for i in $(cat file.txt)
> do
> echo $i
> done

cat file.txt will read file line by line

A for loop is used to execute a block of commands repeatedly for a list of values.

in servers.txt it will have servers ip

for server in $(cat servers.txt)
do
    echo "Connecting to $server"
    ssh ec2-user@$server hostname
done

A for loop in shell scripting is used to iterate over a list of values, files, or numbers and execute a set of commands for each item. It follows the syntax:

for variable in list
do
    commands
done

Common use cases include processing files, automating server tasks, and running commands against multiple AWS resources.

